Rust seam notes (from BE-3): `integration::flows` already provides PKCE S256
+ the loopback listener (ephemeral or pinned port) + device engine;
`providers.rs` `install()` is the registration point; gitlab/snowflake/openai
browser flows extend it directly.

## Phase 2 — the five OAuth variants landed (WIP, green)

- `integration/providers_enterprise.rs` (new, ~1,180 L): gitlab PKCE
  (fixed 8080 redirect, bundled/legacy/env client ids, instance-pin error,
  refresh single-flight via keyed async mutexes, invalid_grant hint
  builder), azure-cli (fake-az testable; method registered only when `az`
  resolves; token JSON with expires_on/expiresOn RFC-1123 parsing via a
  self-contained date parser — no chrono in tree), snowflake external
  browser (48-byte PKCE, `session:role[-encoded]` scopes, Basic
  LOCAL_APPLICATION token-request, env-token refresh bypass),
  openai codex browser (pinned 1455→1457 via new
  `flows::listen_pinned` with /cancel probe + retries; codex authorize
  params; JWT claim account extraction) + headless device-code (usercode →
  poll 403/404 → server-provided verifier exchange against
  `{issuer}/deviceauth/callback`), chatgpt token-sharing connector
  (dynamic client registration via callback `client_id`, nonce/state,
  token-sharing scope enforcement, id_token claim checks iss/aud/exp/nonce/sub).
- `flows.rs`: `pkce_s256_with_bytes`, `jwt_claims`, `which`,
  `listen_pinned` (+cancel probe).
- Exchange seams follow v2's injectable-endpoints pattern
  (`gitlab_exchange_at`, `snowflake_token_at`, `openai_exchange_at`,
  `chatgpt_exchange_at`, `openai_headless_authorize_at`,
  `chatgpt_authorize_at`) — prod wrappers pin the real issuers.
- Tests (12 new, integration suite 17→29, all green): gitlab round-trip
  (fixed-port loopback driven as the browser, S256 challenge-vs-verifier
  consistency recomputed, request shapes, metadata+label), gitlab
  off-gitlab.com rejection, gitlab refresh rotation; azure fake-az
  round-trip + method gating; snowflake token-request shape (Basic header,
  client_id, form refresh fallback), account normalization + role scope
  encodings; openai exchange claims extraction; headless device flow
  round-trip; listen_pinned fallback; chatgpt round-trip (dynamic client,
  nonce echo, request shapes incl. resource), missing-sharing-scope
  rejection, nonce-mismatch rejection.
- Known gap (deliberate): chatgpt id_token RS256/JWKS signature
  verification is NOT implemented (no JWT crate in this workspace); claims
  are validated without signature. Deferred with this note.
- fmt + clippy (pedantic) clean; oc-core nextest 811/811.
